    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0530" n="428" xml:id="pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/845: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan
                        (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-07T12:00:00-05:00">October 7, 1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. Department’s 89, October 6, 1933, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="48" xml:id="d453-f1"/>
                    paragraph numbered 2.</p>
                <p>The Department assumes from your 149<anchor n="49" xml:id="d453-f2"/> that you
                    will discuss this subject only in response to invitation from Hirota for
                    suggestions. In view of likelihood that premature disclosure by Hirota of your
                    conversation on this subject might, by leading to undesirable publicity,
                    prejudice successful intervention by Hirota with Manchukuo, you should impress
                    upon him that if he considers it necessary to inform his colleagues of the
                    conversation he must make it clear to them that it was he who initiated his
                    conversation with you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
